          <Pad Id="d2k02BMV7nJZSg9OxipTJ1" Bounds="85,720,830,190" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="Notes:&#xD;&#xA;- The circles are Point nodes, defined in this patch (Circle, Drag and Translate): one Point in a ForEach over the start positions. Their Position outputs, the centres of the circles, are the Points of the Polyline, so dragging a circle reshapes the chain. Translation sets the start position, Radius the size of the circles.&#xD;&#xA;- Points are in units of the Renderer Space (1 unit = 100 DIP, origin top left), in the space of the parent. A Polyline needs a Stroke Width above 0 and at least two points.&#xD;&#xA;- Cap shapes the two ends of an open chain, so it has no effect while Closed is on. Join shapes the corners; Miter (default) turns into a Bevel at sharp angles, Miter Limit sets where.&#xD;&#xA;- Defaults follow Skia: Cap Flat, Join Miter.&#xD;&#xA;- Points that change every frame cost real time: stay below about 4000 points, or move the shape with Transform and Trim instead.&#xD;&#xA;- Connect it to Renderer [Qt] or a Group [Qt].">
            <p:TypeAnnotation LastCategoryFullName="Primitive" LastDependency="CoreLibBasics.vl">
              <Choice Kind="TypeFlag" Name="String" />
            </p:TypeAnnotation>
            <p:ValueBoxSettings>
              <p:fontsize p:Type="Int32">9</p:fontsize>
              <p:stringtype p:Assembly="VL.Core" p:Type="VL.Core.StringType">Comment</p:stringtype>
            </p:ValueBoxSettings>
          </Pad>
